SUMMARY:Bend of the River (1952)
DTSTART:20260204T023000Z
DTEND:20260204T042000Z
DTSTAMP:20260204T023000Z
UID:cDVMv3ghcy
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 91 mins (1h31m)\n\nReformed border raider Glyn McLyn
 tock (James Stewart) guides a wagon train to Oregon\, but risks it all whe
 n their winter provisions are confiscated by the Portland town boss in Ant
 hony Mann’s stunningly photographed exploration of the greatness\, glory
 \, and fury of the northwest frontier.  Experience the natural grandeur o
 f the Pacific Northwest in this brand new 4K restoration based on the orig
 inal three-strip Technicolor separations.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs
 -and-events/the-pacific-northwestern/bend-of-the-river\n\nEstimated start:
  18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
